<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Layer Confusion: Confusing the Network layer (IP addresses) with the Data Link layer (MAC addresses).</li>
        <li>IDS vs. IPS: Assuming an IDS can block traffic; students must understand that an IDS only alerts, while an IPS acts.</li>
        <li>Proxy Directions: Confusing a forward Proxy (protects the client) with a Reverse Proxy (protects the server).</li>
        <li>Routing Logic: Thinking routers always use the shortest physical path; they use the "optimal" path based on congestion, cost, or speed.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

